# The BAKED half of ~/.ssh/config inside ds-dev, copied into the image at
# /home/dev/ssh_config — one of gsrpi-dev-base's seams. The base's entrypoint writes the
# real ~/.ssh/config from it at start, and docker-child-init.dev.sh then symlinks
# /workspace/.dev-ssh/config over the result when that file exists, which is the normal
# case.
#
# SO WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR is the case where it does not: a fresh clone, or a container
# brought up before `make dev-login` has ever run. It carries NO IdentityFile on purpose.
# The base's own copy of this file names infra's deploy key, and inheriting that would
# have made a first `git push` in here fail with "no such identity:
# /home/dev/.ssh/id_ed25519_infra_deploy" — a message naming another container's
# credential, in a repo that has nothing to do with it. With no identity named, the same
# push fails with "Permission denied (publickey)", which is what is actually wrong.
#
# The real identity is in /workspace/.dev-ssh/config, naming its key by absolute path
# inside the mount; `make dev-login` writes both when it generates a key.

# ── defaults — MUST stay last, and here they are also all there is ──────────
# ssh takes the FIRST value it obtains for each keyword, so a wildcard above a Host block
# silently wins over it. Anything specific belongs in .dev-ssh/config, above this.
Host *
  IdentitiesOnly yes
  ServerAliveInterval 30
  ServerAliveCountMax 3
